# Spec 029 — Hybrid, petrol and diesel cars, and four more EVs

Status: Approved scope, plan in review
Owner: <you>
Related: 022 (engine, catalogue, ingest), 023 (market map, energy filter),
024 (service and maintenance), 028 (translations); owner export of
2026-11-12 (`backend/docs/cars/sources.md`)

## Overview

DriveCheap compares only electric cars today. Newcomers also weigh hybrids
and diesels, and the owner's latest export covers 14 models the catalogue
lacks: 4 electric and 10 hybrid, petrol or diesel. This spec lets the engine
cost a car that burns fuel, adds those models to the catalogue, and feeds
their listings into the market model, so a hybrid or diesel can be ranked
against an EV on the same terms.

## Context

- The engine already has `energy_type` (`ev`, `phev`, `hybrid`, `ice`) on
  options and variants, but every cost path assumes electricity: energy is
  kWh times a charging mix, toll rates are EV rates, and tax rules are read
  for electric cars (023 notes "nothing is invented for hybrids or petrol").
- The 2026-11-12 export holds these models outside the catalogue (listings,
  median asking price):

