## Design

- **Engine.** `VehicleInputs` gains `fuel` (`petrol` | `diesel`, required
  for `hybrid` and `ice`) and `fuel_l_per_100km` (an input with source and
  status). `MarketPolicyInputs` gains `fuel_prices` (petrol and diesel øre
  per litre with P10-P90 ranges). The energy item branches on
  `energy_type`: EVs keep kWh x charging mix unchanged; fuel cars use
  litres x pump price x winter factor. `StochasticBases` gains a litres
  vector and the fuel price and range; the Monte Carlo rescales it with the
  shared price draw, as it does electricity.
- **Rules.** Toll rings gain per-energy rate rows (`ev`, `petrol`,
  `diesel`, `hybrid`); the engine picks the variant's row and fails loudly
  if it is missing. Traffic tax already carries `ice`/`hybrid` rates and
  re-registration bands are energy-blind, so they gain only a weight band
  where a variant is under 1 200 kg.
- **Catalogue.** 14 variants, one per model, the most-listed trim and
  model years in the export (Q4 e-tron 50 quattro, i4 M50, Polestar 2 Long
  Range Dual Motor, Taycan 4 Cross Turismo, Yaris 1.5 Hybrid, Corolla 1.8
  Hybrid, C-HR 1.8 Hybrid, RAV4 2.5 Hybrid AWD-i, Golf 1.0/1.5 eTSI,
  Octavia 2.0 TDI 4x4, Kodiaq 2.0 TDI 4x4, Tiguan 2.0 TDI 4Motion, V60 D3/D4
  by count, Land Cruiser 2.8 D-4D passenger). New-price rows per model year
  in `new_prices.csv`, sourced or `estimate`.
- **Market.** New segments `ev-premium`, `hybrid-small`, `hybrid-suv`,
  `ice-compact`, `ice-suv` with retention priors marked `estimate`.
- **Frontend.** Energy labels and filters for all four types; the energy
  line and option detail read litres and pump price for fuel cars; the
  charging questions carry an "electric cars only" note; strings in en, nb
  and tr.

## Results (2026-11-13, for review)

- **Engine (R1-R4).** `VehicleInputs` has `fuel` and `fuel_l_per_100km`; an
  EV still needs `efficiency_wh_per_km`, and a hybrid or combustion car
  needs both fuel fields, or the scenario fails to load. Energy for fuel
  cars = km x l/100 km x winter factor x pump price; the charging mix is
  ignored. The fuel price draw is the last on the shared Monte Carlo
  stream, so electric results are unchanged (7 EV golden cases pass as
  before). Toll rings carry `fuel_rates` (petrol, diesel; hybrids pay the
  petrol rate in all four rings); a ring without the car's fuel rate fails
  loudly. Re-registration has a light (<= 1 200 kg) table; only the Yaris
  uses it. User overrides now reach dict-held inputs (toll fuel rates).
- **Rules.** Every dated tax rule is now `live`: the 2025 traffic tax was
  6.38 kr/day for fossil cars (the file carried 6.52), and the 2025
  re-registration 12+ band was 1 900 kr (placeholder 1 700).
- **Fuel prices (R2).** SSB 09654 is **CC BY 4.0**, not NLOD. Value = 12-month
  median (petrol 20.08, diesel 20.42 kr/l), range = 24-month P10-P90.
  September 2026 (26.18 / 27.52) sits above that range; noted in the basis.
- **Golden cases (R6).** `g8_hybrid_used_cash` and `g9_diesel_used_cash`,
  worked in `docs/cars/golden/`. Honest note on order: the engine branch
  and the golden cases were written in the same sitting, not strictly
  test-first; both cases matched the hand numbers on the first run.
- **Catalogue (R7).** 14 variants, 36 in total. Fuel use = WLTP x 1.15 for
  real-world driving, winter factor 1.10; all `estimate`. 63 new-price
  rows, 56 inferred; the 7 sourced ones were read in search excerpts, so
  all are `estimate`.
- **Listings (R8).** 904 new listings kept; 89 van registrations skipped.
  Octavia uses the 150 hk 4x4 DSG of 2019 and 2021-24 (no 2020 car was
  listed with it). Land Cruiser: 2 passenger-car listings, estimate only.
- **Market (R9).** Fit on 2 677 listings, 111 cohorts; MAPE 5.7 % (5.0 %
  EV-only), coverage 77.3 %, gate PASS. Weakest segment: `ice-compact`
  coverage 65.9 % (Wilson 55-75 %), on 82 listings.
- **Screens (R10-R12).** Compare rows and option detail show Electric /
  Hybrid / Petrol / Diesel; the charging questions say they apply to
  electric cars only; new labels in en, nb, tr; glossary updated. The
  compare cap rose from 30 to 40 so the whole catalogue still fits one
  scenario (spec 024 R18).
- **Checks.** `pytest` 271 passed (`test_properties.py` blocked locally by
  Windows Application Control, as before); `ruff check`, `ruff format
  --check` clean; `npm run test` 335 passed; `npm run build` OK.
- **Not done.** No headless screenshot tour of the new screens; the
  frontend's offline fixture (`USE_FIXTURE`) still lists electric cars only.

